+      <ol type="1" spacing="normal" indent="adaptive" start="1" pn="section-15-12">
+        <li pn="section-15-12.1">It receives a QUERIEDNOTFOUND response from the superior. In this
+case, the subordinate should abort the transaction.</li>
+        <li pn="section-15-12.2">The superior, on some connection that it initiated, sends a
+RECONNECT command for the transaction to the subordinate. In this
+case, the subordinate can expect to learn the outcome of the
+transaction on this new connection. If this new connection should
+fail before the subordinate learns the outcome of the transaction,
+it should again start sending QUERY commands.</li>
+      </ol>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-15-13">Note that if a TIP system receives either a QUERY or a RECONNECT
 command, and for some reason is unable to satisfy the request (e.g.
